[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5473639915","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121828#issuecomment-5473639915","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121828","id":5473639915,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRkEd6w","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-31T04:17:08Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T04:17:08Z","body":"Can you provide more info about how this fixes the error? Without doing a deep dive, I can't see the connection. \r\n\r\nI think the current logic of `set_code` is such that you only free the pipeline for new code if it compiles, that way you can always fall back on your previous pipelines if shader compilation fails. If this code is necessary, then it will come with a behavioural regression. So I want to be extra certain that this is the correct fix\r\n\r\nIf this code is necessary, then we should just move the existing call to `clear_pipelines()` up before attempting to compile the shader","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5473639915/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5520279293","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121828#issuecomment-5520279293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121828","id":5520279293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSQjG_Q","user":{"login":"Synzorasize","id":60207816,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjA3ODE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60207816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize","html_url":"https://github.com/Synzorasize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T04:18:52Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T04:18:52Z","body":"I think it's trying to free `RID`s which no longer are owned by any of the `RIDOwner`s of the `RenderingDevice` due to the compilation. They're still saved because it had them previously. `pipeline_hash_map.clear_pipelines()` would clear those so the `RenderingDevice` doesn't save them. At least that was my understanding. But I guess from the code, it only frees the version when it fails, otherwise it keeps the previous one. So maybe something else different relating to that can also work?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5520279293/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]